# envfile.py copies this to .env (mode 600) on the VM and fills the secrets; never commit .env.
# Plain NAME=value lines only: no quotes, no $, no spaces (it is data, not a shell script).
# Image versions are pinned in docker-compose.yml (deployed with the commit), not here.
ROOMS_DOMAIN=rooms.hagencylabs.xyz
MATRIX_DOMAIN=matrix.hagencylabs.xyz
# Synapse Admin: proxied by Cloudflare, behind Cloudflare Access (the Caddyfile accepts only Cloudflare).
ADMIN_DOMAIN=admin.hagencylabs.xyz
# PERMANENT: every user ID ends with this (@anna:matrix.hagencylabs.xyz). Change it only before the
# first start. "hagencylabs.xyz" works too, once the apex serves /.well-known/matrix/server.
SERVER_NAME=matrix.hagencylabs.xyz
# Your account's name (e.g. anna for @anna:matrix.hagencylabs.xyz): guard.py's disk/traffic warnings
# go to you from @pm. Empty: they only go to the journal (journalctl -u hagency-guard).
OPERATOR=
# Filled by envfile.py with a random value. Changing it after the first start needs ALTER ROLE too.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# @pm's read-only GitHub App (docs/GITHUB_APP.md): its App ID once registered, and its slug (the
# name in github.com/apps/<slug>). The private key goes in ~/hagency/app/deploy/secrets/github-app.pem
# (mode 600), never here. Empty: @pm doesn't read GitHub on this server.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=hagency-rooms
# The App's Client ID (starts with Iv; public, NOT the client secret): people prove which GitHub account
# is theirs with "Connect GitHub" (tick Enable Device Flow on the App first). Empty: nobody can bind a repo.
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# Optional: only these repos may be chosen (owner/name, comma-separated, no spaces). Empty: any repo that
# has the App installed and that the asker's connected GitHub account can write to (docs/GITHUB_APP.md).
HAGENCY_REPOS=
# Outgoing email (docs/DEPLOY_ORACLE.md, "Sign-up and sign-in"): with all five set, password reset by
# email works, and with HAGENCY_OPEN_SIGNUP=1 below anyone may create an account with an email address
# they confirm. Any one empty or wrong: sign-up stays invite-token only. SMTP_PORT 465 means TLS
# from the start; 587 or 2525 must offer STARTTLS (mail is never sent in the clear). SMTP_FROM is the address only (no name, no spaces).
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@hagencylabs.xyz
# 1: open sign-up once the SMTP settings above are complete. 0 (or missing): invite tokens only; set
# it back to 0 and run deploy.sh again to close sign-up (email for password reset keeps working).
HAGENCY_OPEN_SIGNUP=0
# 1: higher per-person limits while the site is being tested (more rooms, agent codes, joins and agents
# per person: common/test_limits.py). Set it back to 0 and run deploy.sh again before opening to the public.
HAGENCY_TEST_LIMITS=0
# Sign-in with Google and with GitHub (docs/DEPLOY_ORACLE.md, "Sign-up and sign-in"): each
# provider is on once both of its keys are set, independently of the other and of SMTP above. The
# redirect URL to register with both: https://matrix.hagencylabs.xyz/_synapse/client/oidc/callback
HAGENCY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
HAGENCY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
HAGENCY_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
HAGENCY_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The server agent (docs/adr/0025-trial-agent.md): a shared, talk-only agent anyone signed in may use.
# On only with an Ollama Cloud API key (ollama.com, Settings, Keys); empty: off, and the welcome is unchanged.
# Visitors' trial messages go to Ollama Cloud. Caps are messages per UTC day, per visitor and for the server.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
# The models visitors may pick (Ollama Cloud names, comma-separated; the first is the default; "*2": its tokens
# count double against TRIAL_MONTHLY_TOKENS).
TRIAL_MODELS=glm-5.3,kimi-k3.1-pro*2,kimi-k2.7-code,deepseek-v4.1-flash,gpt-oss:120b
TRIAL_PER_VISITOR=50
TRIAL_PER_SERVER=1000
TRIAL_MAX_TOKENS=1500
TRIAL_TIMEOUT_S=90
# Never into pay-as-you-go: trials stop once the plan's month is TRIAL_MAX_SHARE used (all users of this key
# count), or after TRIAL_MONTHLY_TOKENS of their own; one model call at a time, a message waits TRIAL_QUEUE_WAIT_S.
TRIAL_MAX_SHARE=0.5
TRIAL_MONTHLY_TOKENS=5000000
TRIAL_QUEUE_WAIT_S=20
TRIAL_PAUSE_S=900
# Tokens one visitor may use a day (a few throwaway accounts can't spend the month); people from other servers less.
TRIAL_VISITOR_TOKENS=150000
TRIAL_REMOTE_TOKENS=50000
